AUTHORITY AND RECONCILIATION STATUS
Authoritative baseline: AlgoMind_Project_Foundation_Agenda_Detailed_Revised_CFTC.docx, dated 4 September 2026 and revised/approved on 5 September 2026. The earlier AlgoMind_Project_Foundation_Agenda_Detailed.docx is treated as superseded where the revised CFTC version differs. The project conversation additionally establishes the governing architectural decision that MQL5 is the core AlgoMind trading system and Python is only an external-information/data provider for information MQL5 cannot obtain itself.
Supporting engineering evidence retained for gap/status analysis: AlgoMind_Reversion_Testing.xlsx and the stored V38 forensic audit artifacts. These are not allowed to silently override the revised project agenda; they are used to identify existing implementation state, conflicts, and engineering risks.
STRICT NO-INVENTION STATUS: This blueprint deliberately leaves unsupported fields as NOT SPECIFIED, REQUIRES DECISION, ENGINEERING GAP, or CONFLICTING REQUIREMENTS. Recommendations are not incorporated as authoritative requirements.
1. Executive Architecture
AlgoMind is a deterministic, event-driven retail trading research and execution system whose authoritative trading core is MQL5. The system uses MT5-native market/broker information and documented proxy measurements inside the MQL5 core. Python exists only to supply external information that MQL5 cannot obtain or reliably process itself. CFTC/COT is explicitly included as an external/public higher-timeframe futures-positioning source. External information is context, not an independent BUY/SELL command.
The architectural intent preserved from the agenda is modularity: start with MT5 plus local Python communication on a low-resource computer, validate deterministic feature timing and strategy behaviour, then add external data, ZeroMQ and ML only when the relevant contracts and baseline are proven.
